/* The world, drawn once at build time.

   Real coastlines, invented countries. The shapes come from Natural Earth via
   world-atlas, projected with d3-geo's Natural Earth projection into a 1000x500
   viewBox and rounded to a tenth of a pixel — so the front end needs no
   projection library, no TopoJSON client, and no build step. It is a plain
   object of SVG path strings keyed by a numeric territory code.

   The codes are UN M49 numbers and are deliberately opaque. Real country names
   live in TERRITORY_NAMES and are shown ONLY in the Returning Officer's console,
   where somebody has to know which shape they are handing out. No player-facing
   surface ever renders them: on the map a territory is called whatever the power
   holding it is called, and unclaimed land is called nothing at all.

   Antarctica is omitted. Natural Earth 110m, public domain; world-atlas is ISC,
   (c) Michael Bostock. */
